Use random_bytes() and random_int() for secure randomness:

```php
// VULNERABLE: mt_rand for token generation
$token = md5(uniqid(mt_rand(), true));

// SECURE: random_bytes for tokens (PHP 7+)
$token = bin2hex(random_bytes(32));

// SECURE: random_int for OTP (PHP 7+)
$otp = random_int(100000, 999999);

// SECURE: Secure random string generation
function generateSecureToken(int $length = 32): string {
    return bin2hex(random_bytes($length));
}

// SECURE: Secure random from character set
function secureRandomString(int $length, string $chars): string {
    $result = '';
    $maxIndex = strlen($chars) - 1;
    for ($i = 0; $i < $length; $i++) {
        $result .= $chars[random_int(0, $maxIndex)];
    }
    return $result;
}

// SECURE: PHP 8.3+ Random\Randomizer
$randomizer = new Random\Randomizer(new Random\Engine\Secure());
$token = $randomizer->getBytesFromString(
    'abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789', 32
);
```

